//? Title: De Bruijn assembly: an exact toy Euler walk
//? Subtitle: Actual native state and retained original experiments
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Overlapping reads can be represented by their k-mer transitions. An Euler walk
spells a sequence using each observed k-mer occurrence once, but a single contig
exists only when degree balance and connectivity permit it.
)

\toc

> The method

Each k-mer adds a directed multiedge from its(k−1)-byte prefix to suffix. An
Euler trail needs one out−in=1 start and one in−out=1 end, or every degree
balanced for a circuit. Hierholzer follows unused edges, unwinds completed
trails, then reverses the unwinding order. Degree tests plus consuming every
edge establish one complete walk; spelling starts with the first vertex then
appends one byte per edge, giving length edges+k−1. Repeated observations remain
repeated edges.

> Simple worked example

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/velvet_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    namespace a = dm::algorithms;
    namespace g = dm::graphics;
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    auto r = a::velvet_work({"AT", "TC", "CG"}, 2);
    std::print("| actual vertices | edges | actual walk | sequence | complete " "|\n|---|---:|---|---|---|\n|`{}`|{}|`{}`|{}|{}|\n",
               r.vertices, r.edges.size(), r.walk, r.sequence, r.eulerian);
    g::Diagram concept_diagram(48, 1100);
    concept_diagram.node("n0", {0, 0}, "Read edges AT,TC,CG; k2");
    concept_diagram.node("n1", {5, 0},
                         std::format("{} actual consumed edges", r.consumed));
    concept_diagram.node("n2", {10, 0},
                         std::format("Actual sequence {}", r.sequence));
    concept_diagram.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    concept_diagram.save_svg("build/velvet_tiny.svg");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
| actual vertices | edges | actual walk | sequence | complete |
|---|---:|---|---|---|
|`["A", "T", "C", "G"]`|3|`["A", "T", "C", "G"]`|ATCG|true|
\image(figures/velvet_tiny.svg)
// result_end
