> Interpretation and limits

This is a deterministic exact multigraph exercise inspired by de Bruijn
assembly, not the full Velvet genome assembler. It lacks coverage normalization,
tip/bubble removal, sequencing-error correction and multiple-contig output.
Degree/connectivity failure returns explicit eulerian=false and no sequence,
rather than spelling a partial disconnected walk. k must be at least2; shorter
reads contribute no edges.

The complete editable C++ programs save figures locally; results contain
ordinary computed Markdown. Selected counters describe actual producer
operations, excluding validation when stated.

> References

- [Zerbino and Birney, Velvet|https://doi.org/10.1101/gr.074492.107]

